## Enable it

Add the plugin to the generator config, keyed by its id:

```json
"plugins": {
  "<%= id %>": { "path": "<%= destination %>", "options": {} }
}
```

## Layout

- `plugin.yml`: id, version, entrypoint and class
- `lib/<%= id %>.rb`: the entrypoint the host requires
- `lib/<%= id %>/plugin.rb`: `generate(context)`, called once the host has generated its built-in tests
- `lib/<%= id %>/extractor.rb`: this plugin's data for each group
- `templates/`: ERB templates for `InfernoSuiteGenerator::Plugins::TestGenerator` subclasses
- `runtime/`: files the generated tests need at Inferno run time, copied by `context.install_runtime`
- `test/`: this plugin's tests

## Output

Group data goes under `<%= id %>` in `<group dir>/plugins.yml`, and suite data under `<%= id %>` in `<suite dir>/plugins.yml`.

## Test

```bash
bundle exec ruby -Ilib -I<%= destination %>/test <%= destination %>/test/<%= id %>_test.rb
```
